{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8298056",
      "title": "Outsourcing Context & State Into a Separate Provider Component",
      "sourceHash": "e6bbb472444bbb7e2863ca57a0877de14acef6d6ce8a1ee0b9c90c4a0cb2889c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 3.03,
          "en": "Now, as you probably can tell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.03,
          "end": 8.01,
          "en": "this context feature can be very useful for sharing data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.01,
          "end": 11.193,
          "en": "across multiple components in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.27,
          "end": 15.75,
          "en": "But at the moment, the way we're using it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.75,
          "end": 19.77,
          "en": "we still have a pretty bloated app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.77,
          "end": 22.35,
          "en": "Because we're in the end, setting up the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.35,
          "end": 25.2,
          "en": "that should be shared through our context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.2,
          "end": 26.763,
          "en": "in that component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.78,
          "end": 31.53,
          "en": "And whilst this works, you might wanna avoid something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.53,
          "end": 35.4,
          "en": "like this because if your app would become more complex,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.4,
          "end": 38.73,
          "en": "you might have multiple contexts in the same app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.73,
          "end": 40.26,
          "en": "which is possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.26,
          "end": 42.99,
          "en": "And you might have different state values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.99,
          "end": 46.2,
          "en": "that should be shared through those different contexts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.2,
          "end": 47.64,
          "en": "And you would therefore end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.64,
          "end": 50.44,
          "en": "with a lot of logic in your app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.57,
          "end": 54.12,
          "en": "since that is typically your root component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.12,
          "end": 56.76,
          "en": "and has access to all the components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.76,
          "end": 59.343,
          "en": "that might want to use a context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.21,
          "end": 64.77,
          "en": "And therefore there is an alternative approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.77,
          "end": 67.5,
          "en": "an alternative pattern, which you'll see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.5,
          "end": 70.68,
          "en": "in many React projects, which allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.68,
          "end": 75.53999999999999,
          "en": "to get all this context related data management",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.53999999999999,
          "end": 80.13,
          "en": "out of the app component into a separate context component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.13,
          "end": 82.5,
          "en": "And we'll use this pattern here now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.5,
          "end": 86.19,
          "en": "starting in this shopping cart context file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.19,
          "end": 90.87,
          "en": "Because there besides creating and sharing that context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.87,
          "end": 95.07300000000001,
          "en": "we can also create and share a component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.75,
          "end": 101.22,
          "en": "a CartContextPovider component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 101.22,
          "end": 105.50999999999999,
          "en": "Though the name, of course, as always is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 105.50999999999999,
          "end": 108.87,
          "en": "but you, of course, wanna use descriptive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.87,
          "end": 110.49000000000001,
          "en": "component function names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.49000000000001,
          "end": 113.94,
          "en": "And since this component function will be all about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.94,
          "end": 117.42,
          "en": "managing context data and providing that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.42,
          "end": 121.29,
          "en": "to your application and it will be all about context related",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.29,
          "end": 122.61,
          "en": "to the shopping cart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.61,
          "end": 126.303,
          "en": "This sounds like a good name for this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.04,
          "end": 131.1,
          "en": "And now the idea simply is to, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.1,
          "end": 134.55,
          "en": "grab all that state management",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.55,
          "end": 137.37,
          "en": "and context value management code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.37,
          "end": 139.563,
          "en": "from inside the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.94,
          "end": 145.86,
          "en": "So starting here where we create the state with useState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 145.86,
          "end": 149.34,
          "en": "including all these functions that added to the state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.34,
          "end": 154.14,
          "en": "all the way down to where I construct this context value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 154.14,
          "end": 157.6,
          "en": "I'll cut all of that from the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 158.49,
          "end": 160.65,
          "en": "hence making it much leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.65,
          "end": 162.63,
          "en": "And I'll move that into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 162.63,
          "end": 167.63,
          "en": "that CartContextProvider component function like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 168.42000000000002,
          "end": 170.733,
          "en": "so that I'm managing my state in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 172.35,
          "end": 173.37,
          "en": "Now for this to work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.37,
          "end": 177.183,
          "en": "we must import useState in this file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 179.16,
          "end": 182.76,
          "en": "And then with this imported here in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 182.76,
          "end": 185.673,
          "en": "we also must import Dummy Products.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 187.59,
          "end": 192.59,
          "en": "So here I'll import Dummy Products from going up one level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 194.16,
          "end": 197.46,
          "en": "and then there it's this dummyproducts.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 197.46,
          "end": 199.113,
          "en": "here in this starting product.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 200.91,
          "end": 203.82,
          "en": "And with that, we're managing this entire state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 203.82,
          "end": 206.4,
          "en": "and we're constructing this context value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 206.4,
          "end": 207.843,
          "en": "in this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 209.37,
          "end": 212.13,
          "en": "But it's not a real component function yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 212.13,
          "end": 214.17000000000002,
          "en": "we can't use it as such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 214.17000000000002,
          "end": 217.743,
          "en": "because we're not returning anything renderable yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 218.67000000000002,
          "end": 220.2,
          "en": "That of course needs to change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 220.2,
          "end": 223.3,
          "en": "And what I wanna return here is my CartContext",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 224.28,
          "end": 229.28,
          "en": "provider component and the value prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 229.35,
          "end": 232.323,
          "en": "should still be set to this context value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 234.18,
          "end": 237.96,
          "en": "But now this CartContext provider component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 237.96,
          "end": 241.11,
          "en": "should be wrapped around any value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 241.11,
          "end": 245.1,
          "en": "This custom CartContextProvider component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 245.1,
          "end": 246.393,
          "en": "will be wrapped around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 248.1,
          "end": 252.16,
          "en": "So here we should accept and destructure the children prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 253.44,
          "end": 256.12,
          "en": "and then use that down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 257.43,
          "end": 261.51,
          "en": "in our return JSX code to in the end make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 261.51,
          "end": 265.92,
          "en": "that we wrap this CartContext provider with that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 265.92,
          "end": 270.42,
          "en": "around any JSX code around any other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 270.42,
          "end": 274.14,
          "en": "Therefore, this shopping CartContextProvider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 274.14,
          "end": 276.153,
          "en": "component here will be wrapped around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 278.04,
          "end": 281.79,
          "en": "So therefore we can now use this CartContextProvider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 281.79,
          "end": 285.45,
          "en": "component in our app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 285.45,
          "end": 290.113,
          "en": "And there import this from shopping cart context JSX",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 291.18,
          "end": 294.06,
          "en": "this CartContextProvider component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 294.06,
          "end": 296.313,
          "en": "instead of that context object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 297.72,
          "end": 300.27,
          "en": "And we can get rid of useState here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 300.27,
          "end": 303.273,
          "en": "because I'm not managing any state in here anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 304.56,
          "end": 308.61,
          "en": "And we can and should now use this custom component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 308.61,
          "end": 312.483,
          "en": "as a wrapper around header and shop like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 314.28,
          "end": 317.34,
          "en": "So with that, we're still setting up the wrapper here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 317.34,
          "end": 319.35,
          "en": "but we of course got rid of all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 319.35,
          "end": 321.423,
          "en": "that state management logic here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 323.19,
          "end": 326.01,
          "en": "And with that, if you save that and you reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 326.01,
          "end": 330,
          "en": "this app still works as it did before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 330,
          "end": 333.49,
          "en": "I still have my cart here and I can change this cart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 334.38,
          "end": 337.56,
          "en": "but now it works through context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 337.56,
          "end": 340.40999999999997,
          "en": "And we outsourced all this context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 340.40999999999997,
          "end": 343.89,
          "en": "and state management code into a separate component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 343.89,
          "end": 346.32,
          "en": "so that if you had multiple contexts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 346.32,
          "end": 350.37,
          "en": "and multiple pieces of independent data in the same app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 350.37,
          "end": 353.79,
          "en": "you could simply create multiple context files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 353.79,
          "end": 358.08,
          "en": "and therefore keep your app component pretty lean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 358.08,
          "end": 360.96,
          "en": "Because there you would just wrap your components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 360.96,
          "end": 363.573,
          "en": "with that context provider component.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}